WEBVTT

00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:06.345
In the admin menu, Media has two pages.

00:00:06.345 --> 00:00:11.867
Library holds the files, and Profiles holds the presets that resize images.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.524
Profiles lists the media profiles of the site.

00:00:15.524 --> 00:00:20.240
This site has one, named banner, which crops an image to a wide banner.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.241
Under Settings, Media has two entries.

00:00:23.241 --> 00:00:27.745
Options shows the values the library runs with, such as the allowed file

00:00:27.745 --> 00:00:32.885
extensions and the maximum file size, and API chooses how the library authenticates

00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:34.328
with the media API.

00:00:34.328 --> 00:00:36.350
A separate video covers both.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.830
Tools, Features lists what a site can turn on.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:44.171
Searching for media narrows the list to the features that mention it.

00:00:44.171 --> 00:00:46.660
Media itself is enabled on this site.

00:00:47.131 --> 00:00:51.935
Media Slugify rewrites the names of the folders and files you create as

00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:56.553
lowercase words joined by dashes, which keeps their addresses clean.

00:00:56.553 --> 00:01:01.171
Secure Media adds permissions that restrict access to media folders.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:06.508
Other features make uploads resumable and keep every open library up to date

00:01:06.508 --> 00:01:08.650
when files and folders change.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:13.410
Azure Media Storage and Amazon Media Storage store the files in Azure Blob

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:17.159
Storage or in Amazon S3, instead of on the server's disk.

